From de5b6d28bf5dd393216f4d73d291bcaf7ca4b0a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antony Vo <antonyvo@mail.grokbot.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:06:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: support AI SDK 7 and zod 4, forward abortSignal,
 typed errors

- peerDependencies: ai ^6 || ^7, zod ^3.25.76 || ^4.1.8 (same zod range ai itself uses); zod moves from dependencies to peerDependencies so one zod instance is shared with ai.
- execute() forwards ToolExecutionOptions.abortSignal to fetch, rejects before any request when the signal is already aborted, and rethrows AbortError unchanged instead of wrapping it (fixes #22).
- Non-2xx responses throw ExaApiError (status, tag, requestId, retryAfterSeconds, body). The message keeps the 2.x text.
- Optional config.fetch for proxies and tests.
- Tool output is typed as ExaApiResponse instead of unknown.
- Stop sending the deprecated contents.livecrawl: "fallback" on every call; omitting it gives the same API default. Add contents.maxAgeHours (documented on exa.ai/docs/integrations/vercel/ai-sdk but not accepted by 2.1.0 types and dropped at runtime), lite / deep-lite types, people / publication categories, highlights.maxCharacters; mark deprecated options per Exa's OpenAPI spec. livecrawl + maxAgeHours throws up front since the API rejects the combination.

Refs #4 (v7 request in the thread), fixes #22.
